{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/67228","id":3869946997,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde87mqrR1","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/67228","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/67228.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/67228.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/67228","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/67228/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/67228/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/67228/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/statuses/59baaf4a73ada4ac3f48d587e6df01c1d73452c6","number":67228,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add For Loop Analyzer for variables used in closures.","user":{"login":"skrustev","id":3768136,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjgxMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3768136?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev","html_url":"https://github.com/skrustev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skrustev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Add For Loop Analyzer for variables used in closures.\r\n\r\n<!-- Thank you for submitting a pull request to our repo. -->\r\n\r\n<!-- If this is your first PR in the ASP.NET Core repo, please run through the checklist\r\nbelow to ensure a smooth review and merge process for your PR. -->\r\n\r\n- [x] You've read the [Contributor Guide](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) and [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/main/CODE-OF-CONDUCT.md).\r\n- [x] You've included unit or integration tests for your change, where applicable.\r\n- [x] You've included inline docs for your change, where applicable.\r\n- [x] There's an open issue for the PR that you are making. If you'd like to propose a new feature or change, please open an issue to discuss the change or find an existing issue.\r\n\r\n<!-- Once all that is done, you're ready to go. Open the PR with the content below. -->\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nAdd Analyzer that checks `for loop` `iterators` if they are used inside in closures that would results in unexpected runtime behavior. More notable scenarios:\r\n\r\n- Inside `binding` to native elements attributes/events and using lambda expressions.\r\n- Inside `binding` of components attributes/events and using lambda expressions.\r\n- Inside `ChildContent` of components.\r\n- Code in `Nested for loops` should also be taken into account, but variables on inner for loops shouldn't affect upper levels or for loops on same level inside the loop on root level.\r\n- Code in nested other blocks like `if`, `foreach`, `do/while`, `switch` should also be analyzed.\r\n- ? For loop `variables` that are `not incremented` anywhere in the `for loop` shouldn't technically cause an issue, but made things quite more complicated. Or maybe parsing the body twice is ok as well, so it's a bit easier to read? That's why I was not sure if I should include such scenarios, but covered basic checks like `incrementing` them and `assigning` them later on. ?\r\n\r\n\r\nFixes #65234\r\n","labels":[{"id":1164776385,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTY0Nzc2Mzg1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/area-blazor","name":"area-blazor","description":"Includes: Blazor, Razor Components","color":"5319e7","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1592238684,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNTkyMjM4Njg0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/analyzer","name":"analyzer","description":"Indicates an issue which is related to analyzer experience","color":"c0f7f6","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2209519932,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMjA5NTE5OTMy","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/labels/community-contribution","name":"community-contribution","description":"Indicates that the PR has been added by a community member","color":"c2e0c6","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":14553391,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAQzde84A3hEv","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/383","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestone/383","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/milestones/383/labels","number":383,"state":"closed","title":"11.0-preview7","description":"","creator":{"login":"danroth27","id":1874516,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NzQ1MTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1874516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27","html_url":"https://github.com/danroth27","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danroth27/events{/privacy